e def`\n- `h5: side bc = side ef`\n\nThen we need to prove:\n- `|(a─b)| = |(d─e)| ∧ |(a─c)| = |(d─f)| ∧ (∠ a:c:b : ℝ) = (∠ d:f:e : ℝ)`\n\nSo this is essentially the theorem about triangle congruence where if two angles and the included side are equal, then the other sides and angle are equal.\n</think>\n```lean4\nimport Mathlib\n\nopen Real\nopen scoped BigOperators\n\nlemma angle_at_A (a b c : Point) (AB BC AC : Line) (h1 : formTriangle a b c AB BC AC) : (|(a─b)| : ℝ) * (|(a─c)| : ℝ) * Real.sin (∠ a:b:c : ℝ) = (|(a─b)| : ℝ) * (|(a─c)| : ℝ) * Real.sin (∠ a:c:b : ℝ) := by\n  sorry\n\ntheorem example_thm (a b c d e f : Point) (AB BC AC DE EF DF : Line) (h1 : formTriangle a b c AB BC AC) (h2 : formTriangle d e f DE EF DF) (h3 : (∠ b:c:e : ℝ) = (∠ e:f:d : ℝ)) (h4 : (∠ a:b:c : ℝ) = (∠ d:e:f : ℝ)) (h5 : |(b─c)| = |(e─f)|) : |(a─b)| = |(d─e)| ∧ |(a─c)| = |(d─f)| ∧ (∠ a:c:b : ℝ) = (∠ d:f:e : ℝ) := by sorry\n```": 0.1387255942811915}, "cleaned_response": "∀ (a : Point) (b : Point) (c : Point) (d : Point) (e : Point) (f : Point) (AB : Line) (BC : Line) (AC : Line) (DE : Line) (EF : Line) (DF : Line), ((formTriangle a b c AB BC AC) ∧ (formTriangle d e f DE EF DF) ∧ ((∠ a:b:c : ℝ) = (∠ d:e:f : ℝ)) ∧ ((∠ b:c:a : ℝ) = (∠ e:f:d : ℝ)) ∧ (|(b─c)| = |(e─f)|)) → (|(a─b)| = |(d─e)| ∧ |(a─c)| = |(d─f)| ∧ (∠ c:a:b : ℝ) = (∠ f:d:e : ℝ))", "prediction": {"∀ (a : Point) (b : Point) (c : Point) (d : Point) (e : Point) (f : Point) (AB : Line) (BC : Line) (AC : Line) (DE : Line) (EF : Line) (DF : Line), ((formTriangle a b c AB BC AC) ∧ (formTriangle d e f DE EF DF) ∧ ((∠ a:b:c : ℝ) = (∠ d:e:f : ℝ)) ∧ ((∠ b:c:a : ℝ) = (∠ e:f:d : ℝ)) ∧ (|(b─c)| = |(e─f)|)) → (|(a─b)| = |(d─e)| ∧ |(a─c)| = |(d─f)| ∧ (∠ c:a:b : ℝ) = (∠ f:d:e : ℝ))": 1.0}, "groud_truth": "∀ (a b c d e f : Point) (AB BC AC DE EF DF : Line), formTriangle a b c AB BC AC ∧ formTriangle d e f DE EF DF ∧ (∠ a:b:c = ∠ d:e:f) ∧ (∠ b:c:a = ∠ e:f:d) ∧ (|(b─c)| = |(e─f)| ∨ |(a─b)| = |(d─e)|) → (|(a─b)| = |(d─e)|) ∧ (|(b─c)| = |(e─f)|) ∧ (|(a─